  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global emergency response programme (GERP) 2024&#x2013;2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the the Global Emergency Response Programme (GERP), the International Organization for Migration continues to ensure an adequate humanitarian response to the needs of affected populations and host communities in crisis related contexts globally in an efficient and timely manner. The programme comprises three components to achieve three outcomes. The first is determined as a sustained response mechanism and is structured around on-going crises and responses with predictable needs and aims at sustaining the response on-going to provide lifesaving assistance. The second is determined as a rapid response mechanism to respond in a timely manner to sudden onsets and deteriorating circumstances that appear during the period of implementation. The third component is a global prioritization mechanism which is designed to ensure continuity in the support to prioritized countries through softly earmarked funding.</narrative>
  </description>
